{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-11819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/assets/7129baa9dcd41738dbdf04a022b8bbe6a864006896cc76cbee3594ff0a744608.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola with its vertex at $(h,k),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nHere, the vertex has coordinates $(h,k)=(0,-2).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+0)^{2} & =4p(y-(-2)) \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4p(y+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(8,6),$ so we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4p(y+2) \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(6+2) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4p(y+2) \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(2)(y+2) \\\\ {x}^{2} & =8(y+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1c96a935a3d9ce359071b585e1543ab5608a4a69c438f8df8b58be7f1f6bd2e"} {"question" "q-11819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+2)^{2}=8y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=-4(y+2)"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=-8(y+2)"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=4(y+2)"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=8(y+2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}=8(y+2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the upward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(3,-5)$ and which passes through the point $(0,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any upward or downward-opening parabola with its vertex at $(h,k),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nHere, the vertex has coordinates $(h,k)=(3,-5).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4p(y-(-5)) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4p(y+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(0,4),$ so we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4p(y+5) \\\\ (0-3)^{2} & =4p(4+5) \\\\ 9 & =36p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4p(y+5) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{4})(y+5) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =y+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1c96a935a3d9ce359071b585e1543ab5608a4a69c438f8df8b58be7f1f6bd2e"} {"question" "q-11827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+5)^{2}=y-3"] ["math" "(x-3)^{2}=-(y+5)"] ["math" "(x-3)^{2}=-2(y+5)"] ["math" "(x-3)^{2}=2(y+5)"] ["math" "(x-3)^{2}=y+5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-3)^{2}=y+5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/assets/4b30029c03e020e6deacdf6d0728978c5a6d86d88e6bbbf1f8c1a6ec88c278d6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola with its vertex at $(h,k),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nHere, the vertex has coordinates $(h,k)=(4,-2).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n(x-4)^{2}=4p(y+2).\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(0,4),$ so we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2} & =4p(y+2) \\\\ (0-4)^{2} & =4p(4+2) \\\\ 16 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2} & =4p(y+2) \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =4(\\frac{2}{3})(y+2) \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =\\frac{8}{3}(y+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1c96a935a3d9ce359071b585e1543ab5608a4a69c438f8df8b58be7f1f6bd2e"} {"question" "q-11828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+2)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(y-4)"] ["math" "(x-4)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(y+2)"] ["math" "(x-4)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(y+2)"] ["math" "(x-4)^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}(y+2)"] ["math" "(x-4)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(y+2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-11828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-4)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(y+2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the upward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point $(-5,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe're told that the given parabola passes through the point $(-5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-5)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\ 25 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{25}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{25}{8})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1c96a935a3d9ce359071b585e1543ab5608a4a69c438f8df8b58be7f1f6bd2e"} {"question" "q-115434" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115434" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{5}y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{5}y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{8}y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115434" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point $(-4,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe're told that the given parabola passes through the point $(-4,-2),$ so we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 16 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(-2)y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-8y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1c96a935a3d9ce359071b585e1543ab5608a4a69c438f8df8b58be7f1f6bd2e"} {"question" "q-115438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}=-2y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=-8y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=-y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=2y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"} {"question" "q-115438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}=-8y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041773/state.json" "file_sha256" "369ca2be340903dc0e0000bc56499a1eb0bcca276d61420993d688d0f7508be5"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1534 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
